===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|gmw-cfr|alt||most dialects}}
* {{alter|gmw-cfr|oot||westernmost Ripuarian}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gmw-cfr|gmh|alt}}, {{inh|gmw-cfr|goh|ald}} (northern variant of {{m|goh|alt}}), from {{inh|gmw-cfr|gmw-pro|*ald}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|gem-pro|*aldaz}}, from {{inh|gmw-cfr|ine-pro|*altós}}, {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eltós}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂el-|t=grow, nourish}}. Compare {{cog|li|aad}}, {{cog|lb|al}}, {{cog|nl|oud}}, {{cog|nds|old}}, {{cog|fy|âld}}, {{cog|en|old}}. 

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gmw-cfr|/ɔːt/|[ɒːt]}}

===Adjective===
{{head|gmw-cfr|adjective|partitive|'t [[Aods]]}}

# {{lb|gmw-cfr|Kirchröadsj}} [[old]]
#: {{ux|gmw-cfr|'''Aod''' weëde is sjun, mar '''aod''' zieë nit.|Growing '''old''' is great, but being '''old''' isn't.}} 

====Usage notes====
* This is the original form and the secondary form is {{m|gmw-cfr|auw}}. Like other Kerkradish adjectives with secondary forms, the original form, ''aod'', mostly occurs with singular neuter nouns and in predicate form. In other instances the secondary form, {{m|gmw-cfr|auw}}, is preferred.

